{"created": "2026-11-05T13:13:20.757343+00:00", "modified": "2026-11-05T13:21:14.262450+00:00", "id": 23978781, "conceptrecid": "23269974", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23978781", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23269974", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23978781", "metadata": {"title": "The Ansate Cross: Even-Order Realisation and Singly Even Colour Symmetry", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23978781", "publication_date": "2026-11-05", "description": "<p class=\"FirstParagraph\"><span>A pointwise protocol for even-order magic squares. Each cell of an even-order grid receives one of four classes, and its value follows from its coordinates and its class alone.</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\"><span>Version 1.0 held the paper and its twenty-nine scripts; its notes are kept in historique-depot-15.37/, together with the confidence map DEPOT.md (from proved to conjectured) and an English guide. The scripts are in tools/.</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\"><span>The protocol has since become the common framework of the Ansate Cross article, which covers: - the common realisation theorem for even orders; - the strict case I as a special case; - gnomons; - the balanced symmetric families.</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\"><span>This version adds the current text of that article, revision 223 (5 November 2026), in English and French (Markdown, Word, PDF), together with the French revision 220, proof folders 39&ndash;56 with data and logs, and the shared change journal. The independent audit of the Ansate Cross results is in the companion code record 10.5281/zenodo.22866061.</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\"><span>Quick check, with no solver needed: python3 tools/verifie_temoins.py; python3 tools/construction.py; python3 tools/fibres.py.</span></p>\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\"><span>Licences: code under AGPL v3, with a commercial licence on request; article texts under CC BY 4.0; data and generated files under CC BY-NC 4.0.</span></p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": 